{"data":"Agent Blockhall Blockspace Share 2.0.0","licence":"© 2026 bitmap22. All rights reserved. Free to download and use, for people and AI agents; not to be republished or sold without permission (https://github.com/bitmap22/my-ordinal-portal/blob/main/LICENCE).","updated":"2026-11-22T23:47:48Z","what":"How Bitcoin's blockspace splits between the kinds of use, day by day: for each UTC day, the bytes (size), the number of transactions and the fees paid in sats (sats) of each kind, read from every block's own bytes by the Block Manifest's reader. A transaction that is several kinds at once is counted under the first that fits, in this order: Alkanes, runes, BRC-20, SRC-20, Stamps, Counterparty, CRC-20, DMT mints, NAT, TAP, BRC-420, Atomicals, CAT-21, Labitbu, inscriptions, messages, coinbase, consolidations, batch payouts, multisig payments, taproot payments, segwit payments, legacy payments, other payments. \"block header\" is each block's header and transaction count, so the kinds add up to the bytes read (size). notRead lists any block that could not be read: its bytes are not in the day. Fees: each transaction's fee from mempool.space's list (or a copy's), kept for a block only if they add up to what its coinbase pays out (read from its own bytes) less the new coins; fees is the day's total, feesRead the blocks whose fees are in it, feesNotRead the read blocks whose fees are not. Bitcoin only.","kinds":[{"kind":"Alkanes","what":"Alkanes token transactions (they ride inside a rune message, so they come before runes)"},{"kind":"runes","what":"rune etchings, mints and moves"},{"kind":"BRC-20","what":"BRC-20 token inscriptions"},{"kind":"SRC-20","what":"SRC-20 tokens (written as Stamps, so they come before Stamps)"},{"kind":"Stamps","what":"Bitcoin Stamps (data kept in the coins themselves)"},{"kind":"Counterparty","what":"Counterparty transactions that are not Stamps"},{"kind":"CRC-20","what":"CRC-20 tokens (LEAF), the covenant token protocol"},{"kind":"DMT mints","what":"Digital Matter Theory mints (TAP dmt-mint, so they come before TAP and NAT)"},{"kind":"NAT","what":"NAT, the TAP token of Digital Matter Theory"},{"kind":"TAP","what":"other TAP protocol tokens"},{"kind":"BRC-420","what":"BRC-420 inscriptions"},{"kind":"Atomicals","what":"Atomicals"},{"kind":"CAT-21","what":"CAT-21 cats"},{"kind":"Labitbu","what":"Labitbu"},{"kind":"inscriptions","what":"ordinal inscriptions that are not tokens: pictures, text, HTML, bitmaps and every other file"},{"kind":"messages","what":"data written in OP_RETURN that is not a token"},{"kind":"coinbase","what":"each block's first transaction, which pays its miner"},{"kind":"consolidations","what":"three or more coins joined into one"},{"kind":"batch payouts","what":"one payment to ten or more addresses"},{"kind":"multisig payments","what":"payments that spend coins needing several signatures"},{"kind":"taproot payments","what":"payments that spend at least one taproot coin (addresses starting bc1p)"},{"kind":"segwit payments","what":"payments with segwit signatures but no taproot coin (most addresses starting bc1q)"},{"kind":"legacy payments","what":"payments with no segwit signatures at all, the oldest way (addresses starting 1, and some starting 3)"},{"kind":"other payments","what":"any other transaction"},{"kind":"block header","what":"each block's 80-byte header and its count of transactions"}],"firstDay":"2026-10-01","days":[{"day":"2026-10-01","blocks":136,"firstBlock":969370,"lastBlock":969505,"read":136,"notRead":[],"size":216811611,"bytes":{"Alkanes":55039664,"runes":620670,"BRC-20":1550934,"SRC-20":29465,"Stamps":0,"Counterparty":46913,"CRC-20":175191,"DMT mints":0,"NAT":10047,"TAP":4141,"BRC-420":0,"Atomicals":0,"CAT-21":0,"Labitbu":0,"inscriptions":6506353,"messages":3098089,"coinbase":56219,"consolidations":42166635,"batch payouts":15201042,"multisig payments":8300310,"taproot payments":9573117,"segwit payments":69955735,"legacy payments":4465802,"other payments":0,"block he